  "ownership": "Input/output storage must be valid, correctly aligned, live and non-overlapping. Inputs are copied before return; output records use exact byte sizes. Rust owners retain immutable data through release/close/drain; view memory remains live until its owner is released. No arbitrary dangling-pointer safety is claimed.",
  "panic": "Exports catch Rust unwind; an unexpected export panic poisons and drains its Engine. Worker failures preserve actual session/cleanup errors. OOM/native faults may terminate the process.",
  "hostStatus": "Windows exports identity and closed admission outcomes; native Engine support remains pending and must report UNSUPPORTED_HOST, not simulated success.",
  "engineConfiguration": {
    "cachePolicy": "ephemeral",
    "parserIdentity": "TraceParserIdentity; SHA256 and recipe/schema identity remain pinned",
    "publisher": "Normal create requires teamIdentifier, helperCodeIdentifier and parserCodeIdentifier. Fixture create is feature-gated DevelopmentPinned and still checks Mach-O signatures and SHA256.",
    "viewStateBackup": "Optional fixed {backupDirectory}. Requires contentAddressed cache. Backup, native cache and namespace are absolute disjoint roots; requests cannot override roots. Backup is outside cache/LRU."
  },
  "cacheMaintenance": "Engine-scoped bounded background request using only the configured content-addressed held root; no session or request path. Operations are CACHE_INVENTORY, CACHE_MAINTAIN (20/16 GiB), CACHE_PURGE_UNUSED. Poll/result envelope session is zero. Cancel/release/drain and retained result budgets use ordinary request ownership; cancellation after a durable deletion intent may have removed data before returning cancellation.",
  "viewState": "Session-scoped background transport using only the opening held Ready directory and active lease. VIEW_STATE_READ and VIEW_STATE_REMOVE require null input with zero bytes; VIEW_STATE_WRITE copies original format-1 JSON, 1..4194304 bytes, without envelope overhead. All queued/running copied input capacities and rollback pipeline reservations share a fixed 16777216-byte engine admission budget; CAPACITY precedes copying when exhausted and credits refund when commands drop, including rejection/cancel/close/drain/panic. Original closed JSON, traceSHA256, combined flags+marks <=4096, favorites <=4096 and each UTF-8 label/favorite <=4096 bytes are validated by the owner worker before mutation; invalid data is a terminal INVALID_ARGUMENT request error. Read body is {status: sessionScoped|missing|restored|preserved, document only for restored}; write/remove body is sessionScoped|saved|removed|preserved. Unknown/corrupt existing sidecar is preserved; uncached sessions do not persist. Uses ordinary request handles, result ownership/budgets, provenance and cancellation. A cancellation or output failure after durable publication can accompany a committed save/remove; refresh via READ. Ordinary request input remains capped at 1048576 bytes. No caller paths, raw SQL or Swift fallback.",
  "viewStateBackup": "CAP_VIEW_STATE_BACKUP and VIEW_STATE_BACKUP use the ordinary Session request, result, provenance, cancellation, close and drain contracts. Input must be null with zero bytes; destination is fixed viewStateBackup.backupDirectory/rollback. Admission reserves the entire existing 16777216-byte view-state input budget for one bounded native read/encode/publish pipeline, without allocating a dummy buffer; queued/running write inputs and another backup cannot be admitted until this command drops. This is a logical pipeline reservation, not allocator/RSS telemetry. Reads validated format-1 state through the held Session/key lock and publishes an immutable complete private bundle containing view-state.json and receipt.json. Snapshot identity uses domain-separated SHA256 of traceSHA256, parserKey and documentSHA256. Output is {status, receipt}; status is notConfigured|sessionScoped|missing|preserved|backedUp|alreadyBackedUp, receipt is null unless backedUp/alreadyBackedUp. Receipt is closed formatVersion=1, backupIdentifier, traceSHA256, parserKey, documentSHA256 (all lowercase 64-byte digests), documentByteCount=1..4194304, flagCount, persistentMarkCount (combined<=4096), favoriteTrackCount (nullable or 0..4096). Preserve array order, duplicate IDs/favorites and original UTF-8; omit transient marks and retain nullable favorites distinct from empty. No absolute paths, caller destination, raw SQL or automatic restoration. Read snapshot precedes publication; other Sessions can save afterwards. Complete no-replace directory publication and readonly payload verification reject foreign, corrupt, incomplete, linked or writable existing backups. Backup survives LRU/purge. Cancellation/result failure can follow durable publication: retry verifies the exact complete bundle; never infer no change. Request-owned native staging removes only proven prepublication residue, preserves ambiguous postpublication residue and never sweeps unknown owners by age. Swift validates private expected engine/session/request identity and a bounded typed receipt; no public raw decoder.",
  "cpuCatalog": "queryWithDeadline-only closed CpuCatalog query {range,limit:1..4096,activityLimit:1..20000}, under hostContinuousEpochV1 with required absolute deadline. Result is closed {cpus,activity}, both capability-aware EventPages with machine quality. CPU identities are strictly ascending signed Int64, bounded by identities with limit+1 truncation, independent of the first-N scheduling owner sample used for process ordering. Activity truncation never implies CPU directory truncation. The Store retains one 2000000-step VM credit across all identity seeks and activity decoding; cancellation, expired deadline, malformed required identity and budget failure remain failures, never unavailable. No raw SQL or relative deadline reset.",
  "hotSnapshotFacts": "Snapshot format 2 only. Detail source DTOs retain shared canonical presentation and Inspector facts through the viewport owner. Presence flags distinguish absent scalars/text from zero/empty UTF-8; EventKey table/rowID, ipid/itid, semantic duration/open-ended, counter values, priority and frame jankTag remain Int64. Presentation label/category and Inspector name/category are distinct. Density has no Inspector/EventKey. color_rgb is packed 0xRRGGBB from the shared Rust palette. Facts pool is capped at 16 MiB across unique chunks, each Inspector chunk <=4096 without scene truncation. Complete scene/string/JSON retained ownership remains bounded by the existing result budget. Generated ABI 2 and exact digest are required; no format-1 fallback."
}
